  "authoritative_metadata": "manifest.json",
  "title": "Where one row reads the removed line's tie",
  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "On 19 random connected cubic glues of 8 to 10 lines that have a class without solutions (one each), one row of creation between glue lines tells the classes of the glue without a line that tie the removed line's points from those that do not exactly at the lines lying in no two-vertex cut of the incidence graph: it fails at all 16 lines lying in one (two on each of the 8 glues of connectivity 2), where nothing creates anywhere in the tied row or the row colliding with it, and nowhere on the 11 glues of connectivity 3. Each such cut is a pair of lines whose sides each have one more point than lines, one of them K4^(3) without a line. Under the tie, the K4^(3) far side creates at no line meeting the removed line in exactly one point on these 19 glues and on six of the seven trisum glues, but on the 12-line trisum glue of seed 1 it does, for 8 of its 12 removed lines; and that silence with the degenerate entries does not tell every class apart on every 3-connected glue. No single near point makes K4^(3) create, and a one-point local relation is degenerate exactly when its point is tied to the gluing line.",
